    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0220" n="184" xml:id="pg184"/>

                <head>66. Oral Reply From the Soviet Ambassador (Dobrynin) to Secretary of State
                        Rusk<anchor n="1" xml:id="d66-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1965-01-25">January 25, 1965</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>An underground nuclear explosion was indeed carried out in the Soviet
                        Union.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d66-f2"/> This explosion was carried out deep
                    down underground. The quantity of radioactive debris that leaked into the
                    atmosphere was, however, so insignificant that a possibility of its fallout
                    outside the territorial limits of the Soviet Union should be excluded. Thus, the
                    underground explosion that was carried out does not affect the provisions of the
                    Treaty Banning Nuclear Weapons Tests in the Atmosphere, in Outer Space and
                    Underwater.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
